;; app.registry.tests — the platform's own self-tests for the `registry`
;; package's fn-defs (docs/TESTS.md). Ordinary fn-defs in a `tests`
;; namespace: every free arg bound, `:assert` / `:assert-eq` over the
;; subject, passing when they do not throw.
;;
;; Everything here is PURE: the compositions that read the registry
;; through `:query-entities` (`:marketplace-review-map`,
;; `:marketplace-index-groups`, `:storefront-rows`, `:list-package-versions`,
;; …) are tested by re-binding their data slot to literal rows, which drops
;; the `:db` read from the closure — the transform is the subject, not
;; the query. Compositions whose reads sit BELOW a private (the request
;; filters `:marketplace-listing` / `:storefront-listing`, the item pages,
;; the moderation queue, `:fetch-package-version`, `:fork-package`) cannot
;; be re-bound from outside and stay untested here — they are covered by
;; the HTTP-level suites.
;;
;; String-keyed maps (the review / install aggregates) are built with
;; `:zipmap` at run time: a `{:value {"p" …}}` literal round-trips through
;; jsonb with its keys keywordised.

